{id:'station',name:'Last Train Station',color:'#5e6c68',clue:'The ticket has tomorrow’s date. The departure board lists your childhood address.',choices:[['Board the last train','The passenger','You board the train. Every passenger has your face at a different age. At the next stop, you finally recognise the person waiting for you.'],['Take the signal operator’s chair','The signal keeper','You change the signal to red. The train never arrives at the house. Every night, you keep one more family from boarding.']]},
{id:'library',name:'Municipal Archives',color:'#776d57',clue:'The register lists your death on every page. One blank line remains beneath Mother’s name.',choices:[['Erase your entry','The unwritten','You erase your entry from the register. Outside, nobody remembers the house. You do not remember it either—until you find the key in your pocket.'],['Sign as the new archivist','The archivist','You sign your name at the desk. The books settle. Every lost child has a place in the catalogue now. One shelf is reserved for you.']]},
{id:'cinema',name:'Orpheum Cinema',color:'#69565a',clue:'The projector plays your kitchen. On screen, Mother is about to open the spare room.',choices:[['Cut the final reel','The missing scene','You cut the film before the door opens. The screen turns white. When you walk home, the hallway ends where it always should have.'],['Step into the screen','The understudy','You step into the picture. Mother looks up from the kitchen table. Somewhere behind you, an audience begins to applaud.']]},
{id:'clinic',name:'St Agnes Clinic',color:'#69766b',clue:'A case file describes a patient split into a memory and a body. The consent form is unsigned.',choices:[['Destroy the case file','Discharged','You destroy the file. The ward doors unlock. You and Mother leave together, but the scar on your palm has two lifelines.'],['Accept the offered treatment','The quiet ward','You sign the consent form. Your fear disappears first. Then your name. A nurse closes the curtains around a bed that has always been yours.']]},
{id:'chapel',name:'Chapel of the Echo',color:'#736b61',clue:'The bell has no clapper. A prayer tucked inside says: “Speak the name you were given before the room.”',choices:[['Ring the bell with your voice','The returned name','You speak your own name into the bell. The city answers in Mother’s voice. Every locked door opens, and none of them lead back to the spare room.'],['Stay for the midnight vigil','The last candle','You light the final candle. The shadows kneel around you. You promise to keep the light burning until every forgotten child comes home.']]},
{id:'radio',name:'North Street Radio',color:'#5f677b',clue:'The emergency frequency repeats a warning in your voice. A second microphone is warm.',choices:[['Broadcast a warning','The warning','You warn the city never to open an unfamiliar door. All around you, radios click off. At home, Mother puts down the spare key.'],['Answer the voice on air','The transmission','“I’m here,” you say. Your voice escapes through every radio in the city. You can never return to your body, but no one will be alone in the house again.']]}
